                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="vDF8wKPaYGh-nEyzNlaT-65" value="LLM" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontStyle=1;fontSize=16;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1762" y="-540" width="40" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="vDF8wKPaYGh-nEyzNlaT-66" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;v1.4.0 Data Retrieval Improvement&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;This update focuses on improving the data retrieval portion of our application. Part of the reason for inaccurate results, could stem from inaccurate retrieval methods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;This would also be an opportunity to reformat the parameters given to users for tuning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;As it stands, users are given the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;- Cosine sim threshold&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;- Number of chunks returned&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;as their tunable parameters. However this relates to the problem that we have stated in our documentation, in that there are some instances where users are not able to know what has been or has not been shown, making tuning all the more ambiguous&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: rgb(32, 32, 32); font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe WPC&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;Hence, we decided to make it a little more unambiguous, by giving levels of retrieval instead. Known as Low, Medium, High and super High. This update focuses only on low and medium, with low being the same as our current legacy implementation&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fontSize=16;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="277" y="-750" width="685" height="420" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
